From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 08:43:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Sisong 2.16-4: it compiles with the compiler this machine has

Run > Compile This File ran "g++" and told its reader "there is no
compiler on this machine" while clang and lld sat in /boot/system/bin
(patch 0077). The editor now builds with clang++ for C++ and clang for
C, moves an old g++ default in a settings file on, and says which
compilers the machine has when a command really is missing. It also
gains File > Examples, which copies one of the examples (patch 0078)
into ~/examples and opens it, because they ship on a read-only volume
and the compiler must be able to write beside the source.

ProseApps a38255f8ee28c4895c32741c111571a8b5a71392.

